{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00361",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.97,
      "end_seconds": 4.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Excuse me, doctor, should I sit here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.49,
      "end_seconds": 9.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Of course, put it down anywhere. So, how can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 10.27,
      "end_seconds": 13.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Hmm, doctor, thank you for seeing us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.55,
      "end_seconds": 17.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. We'll go through it together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 19.51,
      "end_seconds": 24.63,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "I'm here because of diarrhoea. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.74,
      "end_seconds": 27.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "And when did that start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.09,
      "end_seconds": 36.3,
      "duration_seconds": 8.21,
      "text": "I've had it since Friday. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.82,
      "end_seconds": 44.83,
      "duration_seconds": 7.01,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.24,
      "end_seconds": 54.22,
      "duration_seconds": 8.98,
      "text": "I'd say all the time. I notice it more with eating and drinking milk. Moderate, I'd say. So, I've been feeling weak too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.67,
      "end_seconds": 57.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Has anything about your daily routine changed lately?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.05,
      "end_seconds": 73.78,
      "duration_seconds": 14.73,
      "text": "Not really, the days are pretty much the same, work and home, and I've been trying to fit appointments in around my schedule, which isn't always easy, so I'm glad we could find a time today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.16,
      "end_seconds": 75.11,
      "duration_seconds": 0.95,
      "text": "Any black stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.67,
      "end_seconds": 79.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "Oh, uh, not at all, no black stools."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.28,
      "end_seconds": 84.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Any recent antibiotics, blood in the stool or weight loss at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.49,
      "end_seconds": 88.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Oh, you know, no, none of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.34,
      "end_seconds": 92.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Alright, how about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.28,
      "end_seconds": 96.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "No, uh, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.63,
      "end_seconds": 99.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Is the room warm enough for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.93,
      "end_seconds": 102.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "It's perfect, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.31,
      "end_seconds": 104.26,
      "duration_seconds": 0.95,
      "text": "What about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.11,
      "end_seconds": 109.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "I don't drink at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.45,
      "end_seconds": 111.42,
      "duration_seconds": 0.97,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.48,
      "end_seconds": 114.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.85,
      "end_seconds": 117.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Are you on any tablets or medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 118.92,
      "end_seconds": 124.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "Right, it's Glycomet, 500 milligrams, twice a day for my sugar, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.35,
      "end_seconds": 126.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 127.84,
      "end_seconds": 137.96,
      "duration_seconds": 10.12,
      "text": "About two years. She takes Tiotropium inhaler, once a day. She is on ORS, a few times a day, I give it to her."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.89,
      "end_seconds": 142.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.03,
      "end_seconds": 146.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "I'm allergic to peanuts, I get hives."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.41,
      "end_seconds": 154.89,
      "duration_seconds": 6.48,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.35,
      "end_seconds": 156.22,
      "duration_seconds": 0.87,
      "text": "Yes, diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.12,
      "end_seconds": 160.82,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "I see."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.47,
      "end_seconds": 167.88,
      "duration_seconds": 6.41,
      "text": "COPD, for about a year. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.53,
      "end_seconds": 174.78,
      "duration_seconds": 6.25,
      "text": "Okay, diabetes, that's already on your record. Good to know. I'll take a few measurements first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.44,
      "end_seconds": 183.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "Hold still for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.18,
      "end_seconds": 200.95,
      "duration_seconds": 6.77,
      "text": "Okay: weight 67 kilos, pulse 105, height 175 centimetres, saturation 97 percent, blood pressure 116 over 76, temperature 38.9."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.29,
      "end_seconds": 206.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.8,
      "end_seconds": 209.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "We'll put it in context in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.62,
      "end_seconds": 215.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.71,
      "end_seconds": 217.41,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.18,
      "end_seconds": 221.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Hold your arm out like this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.47,
      "end_seconds": 241.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "Bowel sounds are active, tummy is soft with mild tenderness all around."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.99,
      "end_seconds": 246.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "A little pressure here, tell me if it's tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.95,
      "end_seconds": 263.91,
      "duration_seconds": 0.96,
      "text": "You're mildly dehydrated."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.33,
      "end_seconds": 292.36,
      "duration_seconds": 26.03,
      "text": "Alright, all done, thank you, please sit down. Thank you for that. I'll write up what I found in a moment, and then I'll tell you what I think is going on. Okay, so my impression is this: It fits best with acute gastroenteritis. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had diarrhoea, since Friday, moderate, and no blood in the stool or weight loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 292.92,
      "end_seconds": 294.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.17,
      "end_seconds": 323.4,
      "duration_seconds": 28.23,
      "text": "We should do a stool test for diarrhoea. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. I'd like you to take zinc, 20 milligrams, once a day, for ten days. That should help with diarrhoea. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well. Stick to bananas, rice, toast, curd, and avoid milk and oily food till it settles. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.36,
      "end_seconds": 334.51,
      "duration_seconds": 10.15,
      "text": "If you pass blood or can't keep anything down, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department. Come back if it's not better in three days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 335.38,
      "end_seconds": 339.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Sure, uh, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.44,
      "end_seconds": 344.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Just to confirm, what are the next steps as you understand them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 345.37,
      "end_seconds": 356.79,
      "duration_seconds": 11.42,
      "text": "So, um, I take the zinc, 20 milligrams, once a day and come back if it's not better in three days. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 357.69,
      "end_seconds": 361.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 362.31,
      "end_seconds": 365.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "No, uh, you've explained it well. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}